// =============================================================================
// Engrisk — PostgreSQL domain model (design artifact, not a migration)
// Revision 4.2: workload-based mixed BIGINT/UUID identifiers (random 8-digit BIGINT user IDs); integrity-first optimization of the approved Core V2 versioned content graph
// (engrisk_core_content_v2.dbml); remaining domains reviewed for safe consolidation without compromising integrity.
// Companion docs: apps/ux_preview/product_flow.md, content_studio_spec.md,
// backend/docs_design/api_*.md (API docs still use revision-1 table names; see rename map).
// PostgreSQL 14 design target. Requires @dbml/cli + PostgreSQL DDL validation before migration.
// =============================================================================

Project engrisk {
  database_type: 'PostgreSQL'
  Note: '''
# Engrisk data model (revision 4.2)

**Scope.** TOEIC + IELTS practice, mock exams, review, AI tutor/evaluation, learner uploads,
Content Studio, community contributions — and using the same content core, courses, lessons,
curated collections, AI-generated content and adaptive practice.
Phase 1 runs as ONE logical product (the platform tenant). The model is multi-tenant-ready.

## Domains (TableGroups) — 40 tables
1. identity_access  (8) global identity, unified action tokens and role assignments, RBAC
2. tenancy          (3) tenants, memberships, feature entitlements
3. media            (2) object-storage files + learner source materials
4. reference        (2) exam types, skill taxonomy
5. content_graph    (7) items, immutable versions, placements, media links/timelines,
                         protected answer specs and skill tags
6. content_ecosystem(4) access grants, credits, ratings, reports
7. content_workflow (3) imports, submissions, unified feedback and review-decision events
8. learning         (6) goals, attempts, responses, annotations, evaluations, scores
9. ai               (3) AI-run ledger, conversations and messages
10. platform        (2) async jobs, idempotency keys

**Lean-first policy.** The two statistics tables in V3 were derived caches, not authoritative facts.
Delivery manifests are immutable media_assets (deterministic keys) pinned by attempts.
One-time tokens and role assignments are reused across account/tenant workflows.
Review decisions are append-only content_comments events. Re-introduce materialized read
models when a measured performance requirement warrants it, not by default.

## Content model = versioned content graph (Core V2)
- `content_items` is the stable logical identity (exam, section, block, stimulus, question,
  collection; later course, module, lesson…). It owns tenant, visibility, access tier,
  provenance, owner, archival and the `current_published_version_id` pointer. NO parent_id.
- `content_item_versions` owns everything that is versioned: schema_key (renderer/domain
  contract), title, learner-visible `body`, behavioural `settings`, difficulty, points,
  scoring policy, origin/AI provenance, publication state. Published versions are immutable.
- `content_item_relations` are ordered placements parent VERSION → child ITEM (+ exact child
   version when pinned). Placement ID is stable inside that parent version; a child may be
   placed multiple times in one tree, so attempts must identify served occurrence.
  Exam subtrees are pinned only; collections may bind `latest_published`.
- Protected data never sits in learner-visible `body`: answer keys/rubrics/explanations live
  in `content_answer_specs`; transcripts and cue maps live in `content_media_timelines`.
- Typical TOEIC tree: exam → section (L, R) → section (P1..P7) → block (Part 3 conversation)
  → stimulus (audio clip) + questions. Standalone questions (Part 2/5) hang off a section.
  IELTS: exam → section (Listening P1..P4 / Reading passages / Writing tasks) → block → …
  A course later: course → module → lesson → stimulus/question/exam. Same tables.
- A practice set that picks a subset of a passage's questions is a new block placing the SAME
  stimulus and question items; nothing is copied.
- Publishing a root compiles a pinned, learner-visible `media_assets` object (purpose=delivery_manifest).

## Tenant isolation strategy
- **Global (no tenant_id):** users, auth_*, permissions, system roles, exam_types, skills.
- **Tenant-owned roots carry NOT NULL tenant_id:** content items/versions, media, attempts,
  goals, imports, submissions, jobs, AI runs, conversations.
- **Children inherit** tenant via parent unless tenant_id is needed for a composite FK.
- **Composite FKs** `(tenant_id, x_id) → parent(tenant_id, id)` keep authoring graphs, media
  links and workflow rows inside one tenant.
- **Learner data → membership:** `(tenant_id, user_id) → tenant_memberships(tenant_id, user_id)`.
- **Intentional cross-tenant edges (plain FKs, checked by service + future RLS):**
   learner records → published content of the platform tenant (visibility public) or content
  granted via `content_access_grants`; relation children → explicitly granted/public items.
  Content never references learner data.
- **Future RLS:** `SET LOCAL app.tenant_id / app.user_id`; policies on tenant-owned roots plus
  a read policy for published public/granted content; children use EXISTS(parent) policies.

## Default platform tenant
A seeded tenant (kind = platform, slug = 'engrisk') owns global content and all B2C learners'
memberships, so `tenant_id IS NULL` never means "global".

## Versioning & historical consistency
- Editing published content = new version (based_on_version_id → source). Old parents and
  old attempts keep pointing at the old version.
- Attempts pin the root version (`attempts.content_version_id`) and immutable served manifest;
   responses pin the question version AND served occurrence, even for repeated questions.
   Saves use optimistic row revisions, not device-dependent last-write-wins.
   Scores store the exact scoring-policy key that produced them.
- AI-generated and imported content use the same tables (origin + ai_run_id / content_imports).

## Sensitive data
- Protected (server-only until the disclosure policy allows): content_answer_specs.*,
  content_media_timelines.cues / transcript_segments, content_comments of kind flag or review_decision,
  content_reports.attempt_id. Enforce in API DTOs; optionally column/table GRANTs for a
  read-only delivery role that cannot read protected tables at all.
- Only password HASHES (argon2id) and token HASHES are stored. OAuth tokens are not stored.
- Binary files live in object storage (R2 prod / MinIO local); PostgreSQL stores keys + metadata.

## Conventions
- **ID strategy:** users.id = random 8-digit BIGINT; transactional/catalog IDs (tenants, roles, attempts, responses, evaluations, scores, ai_runs, conversations) = PostgreSQL-assigned BIGINT; content graph, media, source materials, auth sessions and async jobs = UUID.
  BIGINT identifiers are assigned by the PostgreSQL database using identity/sequence (DBML `increment`); only users.id uses secure random-8 function. Child FK columns always match the referenced PK type. Composite PKs retain member-specific types.
  jobs.target_key is TEXT because targets can have heterogeneous UUID/BIGINT IDs; handler validates type + key, NOT a foreign key. No implicit numeric casts or blind UUID parsing.
  snake_case, plural table names, FK = `<referenced_entity>_id`, or `<role>_<entity>_id` when
  the role matters (owner_user_id, parent_version_id, question_version_id).
- timestamptz everywhere, named `*_at`; actors `*_by_user_id`; booleans `is_*`; counters
  `*_count`; durations `*_ms` / `*_seconds`; ordering `position` (ascending within its scope).
- Vocabulary columns:
  - `kind`   immutable category of a row (content kind, asset kind, job kind, …)
  - `schema_key` + `schema_version`  the typed JSON contract of a content version payload
  - `status` lifecycle state;  `mode`  behaviour chosen per run (attempt mode)
  - `role`   function of a participant or attachment in a relationship (credit, asset link)
  - `purpose` why a file or AI run exists (drives access/cost policy)
  - `code`   stable identifier of a row in a seeded catalog table (roles, permissions, skills)
  - `*_key`  reference to a code-defined artefact that is NOT a table (scoring_policy_key,
             rubric_key, schema_key, prompt_key, feature_key, section_key)
  - `settings` authored configuration that changes behaviour; `metadata` system-observed
    descriptive facts; `body` learner-visible document payload.
- **Enum vs registry:** DBML Enums are used for closed state machines and security-relevant
  values (implemented as `text + CHECK`, cheap to evolve). Open, extensible vocabularies —
  content kind, schema_key, relation slot, asset link role, job kind, conversation kind,
  feature keys — are `text` validated against a code registry, so new content types and
  features need no schema change.
- JSONB only for (a) schema_key-typed document payloads validated by Pydantic/JSON Schema,
  (b) immutable snapshots, (c) small config blobs read as a whole. Never for relational facts
  that are joined, filtered or aggregated (those get columns/tables).
- Partial unique indexes are documented in index notes (DBML cannot express WHERE).

'''
}

// =============================================================================
// ENUMS (closed value sets — implemented as text + CHECK)
// =============================================================================

Enum user_kind {
  guest [note: 'Anonymous learner created on first practice; no auth identity yet']
  registered
}

Enum user_status {
  active
  suspended
  deleted [note: 'Soft-deleted + PII scrubbed; row kept for referential history']
}

Enum auth_provider {
  password
  google
  apple [note: 'Future']
  microsoft [note: 'Future']
  oidc [note: 'Future enterprise SSO per tenant']
}

Enum action_token_purpose {
  email_verification
  password_reset
  tenant_invitation [note: 'Single-use email-bound invitation to tenant with assigned role']
}

Enum tenant_kind {
  platform [note: 'Exactly one: Engrisk itself. Owns global content and B2C memberships']
  organization [note: 'Phase 4: language centers, schools, companies']
}

Enum tenant_status {
  active
  suspended
  archived
}

Enum membership_status {
  active
  suspended
  left
}

Enum role_scope {
  platform [note: 'Granted via role_assignments; cross-tenant powers']
  tenant [note: 'Granted via role_assignments; powers inside one tenant']
}

Enum asset_kind {
  audio
  image
  video [note: 'Future (lesson videos); storage pipeline identical']
  document [note: 'PDF, CSV, ZIP packages, JSON manifests']
}

Enum asset_purpose {
  content_media [note: 'Audio/images/documents placed in content versions (stimuli, section tracks, lesson media)']
  cover [note: 'Cover image of a catalog item (exam, course, collection)']
  source_material [note: 'Learner/teacher upload used for AI generation (source_materials)']
  response_media [note: 'Learner answer media, e.g. speaking recordings']
  branding [note: 'Tenant logos']
  import_package [note: 'ZIP package (manifest + audio + images) uploaded to Content Studio import']
  import_report [note: 'System-generated CSV validation report of an import']
  delivery_manifest [note: 'Compiled learner-visible JSON of a published root version']
}

Enum asset_status {
  pending_upload
  processing [note: 'Upload verified; scan / probe / transcode running']
  available
  quarantined [note: 'Failed malware/content scan or checksum verification']
  deleted
}

Enum rights_basis {
  own_work
  licensed
  public_domain
  personal_study_only [note: 'May never be published beyond the owner']
}

Enum material_status {
  uploaded
  processing
  ready
  failed
  rejected [note: 'Policy/safety rejection']
}

Enum skill_area {
  listening
  reading
  writing
  speaking
}

Enum content_visibility {
  private [note: 'Owner only (owner_user_id)']
  tenant [note: 'Members of the owning tenant']
  public [note: 'Platform tenant only: whole platform catalog']
}

Enum access_tier {
  guest [note: 'Playable without an account']
  registered
  premium [note: 'Requires entitlement (future monetization)']
}

Enum content_provenance {
  engrisk_original [note: 'Authored by the Engrisk content team (platform tenant only). Badge "Engrisk Original"']
  tenant_authored [note: 'Authored by an organization (teacher / tenant content team)']
  community [note: 'Contributed by a learner, published by the platform after moderation; always credited']
  licensed_partner [note: 'Material licensed from a publisher partner under contract (P4)']
}

Enum content_origin {
  human
  imported
  ai_generated
}

Enum version_status {
  draft [note: 'Only mutable state']
  in_review [note: 'Frozen while a submission or AI-content review decides']
  scheduled [note: 'Passed publish validation; frozen; promoted to published at publish_at']
  published [note: 'Immutable. Old published versions stay valid for every parent/attempt pinning them']
  retired [note: 'Immutable; not selectable for new placements or attempts; history intact']
}

Enum binding_mode {
  pinned [note: 'Exact child version; mandatory inside exam/assessment subtrees']
  latest_published [note: 'Child resolved to its current_published_version_id at read time (collections, course shelves)']
}

Enum submission_status {
  submitted [note: 'Frozen version queued; auto-checks running/finished, no reviewer yet']
  in_review [note: 'Assigned to a reviewer']
  changes_requested [note: 'Back to contributor with anchored comments; resubmission = new round']
  approved [note: 'Version published (or scheduled). Terminal']
  rejected [note: 'Terminal; reason_code mandatory. Appeal = new submission referencing this one']
  withdrawn [note: 'Contributor withdrew before decision. Terminal']
}

Enum review_decision {
  approve
  request_changes
  reject
}

Enum import_status {
  uploaded [note: 'Package stored (media_assets.purpose = import_package), scan pending']
  validating [note: 'Manifest parsing + per-row validation + asset matching']
  validated [note: 'Report ready; user may create the draft — rows with errors are skipped, warnings kept']
  failed [note: 'Package unreadable / malware / package-level errors']
  completed [note: 'Draft root item + version + children created']
}

Enum credit_role {
  author
  narrator [note: 'Voice actor of listening audio']
  editor
  reviewer [note: 'Moderator who approved; shown only if they opt in']
  translator [note: 'Vietnamese explanations']
}

Enum contribution_license {
  platform_nonexclusive [note: 'Contributor keeps copyright; grants Engrisk a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free licence to host, adapt (format/fix) and distribute; revocable for future distribution']
  cc_by_4_0 [note: 'Creative Commons Attribution 4.0; attribution via content_credits']
}

Enum comment_kind {
  review_decision [note: 'Immutable moderator decision event, linked to a submission round']
  comment [note: 'Human discussion (reviewer, contributor, co-author)']
  flag [note: 'Quality finding from a validator or AI quality check; staff/author-only']
}

Enum report_status {
  open
  resolved
  dismissed
}

Enum attempt_mode {
  practice [note: 'Instant feedback allowed, pausable, listening replay allowed']
  mock [note: 'Exam rules: server deadline, no feedback until submit, single audio play']
}

Enum attempt_status {
  in_progress
  submitted [note: 'Objective grading done; subjective evaluations pending']
  completed [note: 'All scores final for this attempt']
  abandoned
}

Enum submit_reason {
  learner
  time_expired
}

Enum annotation_kind {
  highlight [note: 'Learner-selected text range in a stimulus']
  note [note: 'Highlight + learner note text']
}

Enum evaluator_kind {
  ai
  human
}

Enum evaluation_status {
  pending
  completed
  failed
  superseded
}

Enum score_kind {
  raw [note: 'Points earned / max points. Deterministic']
  scaled_estimate [note: 'Exam scale via unofficial conversion table (TOEIC 10–990, IELTS band)']
  ai_estimate [note: 'AI-evaluated band for Writing/Speaking. Never official']
}

Enum goal_status {
  active
  achieved
  archived
}

Enum execution_status {
  queued
  running
  succeeded
  failed
  cancelled
}

Enum ai_purpose {
  explanation
  tutor_reply
  writing_evaluation
  speaking_evaluation
  transcription
  question_generation
  audio_alignment [note: 'Forced alignment of audio ↔ transcript → content_media_timelines']
  speech_synthesis [note: 'TTS for listening drafts']
  originality_check [note: 'Similarity / copyright screening of submissions']
  quality_check [note: 'AI quality flags → content_comments (kind flag)']
  content_assist [note: 'Draft/translate explanations, alt text, skill-tag suggestions']
  material_extraction [note: 'OCR / structure extraction from source materials']
}

Enum message_role {
  user [note: 'The learner']
  assistant [note: 'AI reply; always carries ai_run_id']
  system [note: 'Context/grounding notices shown in the thread']
}

// =============================================================================
// 1. IDENTITY & ACCESS (global)
// =============================================================================

Table users {
  id bigint [pk, default: `public.generate_random_user_id()`, note: 'Globally unique random 8-digit number (10000000..99999999), NOT sequence. PK and user FK target; database PK enforces uniqueness, callers retry on ID collision.']
  kind user_kind [not null, default: 'registered']
  status user_status [not null, default: 'active']
  email citext [note: 'Primary contact/login email. NULL for guests. Unique when not null']
  email_verified_at timestamptz
  display_name text
  avatar_url text [note: 'External URL (e.g. Google picture); no binary']
  locale text [not null, default: 'vi', note: 'BCP 47 UI language (vi | en), same code the API exposes']
  timezone text [not null, default: 'Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh']
  preferences jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: '{"study_reminder":{"enabled":true,"time":"20:00"}} — small personal settings read as a whole']
  platform_permissions_version integer [not null, default: 1, note: 'Bumped on role_assignments change; part of the access-token ver claim']
  registered_at timestamptz [note: 'Set when a guest converts or a user signs up']
  last_seen_at timestamptz
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    email [unique, name: 'uq_users_email', note: 'Partial: WHERE email IS NOT NULL']
    (kind, created_at) [name: 'ix_users_guest_cleanup', note: 'Partial: WHERE kind = guest — expire unconverted guests']
  }

  checks {
    `kind = 'guest' OR email IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_users_registered_has_email']
    `id BETWEEN 10000000 AND 99999999` [name: 'ck_users_id_random8']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Global person identity. Holds NO credentials, NO roles, NO tenant data.
Guest → account conversion keeps the same 8-digit users.id (kind guest → registered + new
auth_identity), so attempts made as a guest need no data migration.
'''
}

Table auth_identities {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  user_id bigint [not null, ref: > users.id]
  provider auth_provider [not null]
  provider_subject text [not null, note: 'Google "sub"; for password = normalized email']
  provider_email citext [note: 'Email asserted by the provider at last login']
  password_hash text [note: 'argon2id hash. Only for provider = password']
  last_used_at timestamptz
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (provider, provider_subject) [unique, name: 'uq_auth_identities_provider_subject']
    (user_id, provider) [unique, name: 'uq_auth_identities_user_provider', note: 'One identity per provider per user']
  }

  checks {
    `(provider = 'password') = (password_hash IS NOT NULL)` [name: 'ck_auth_identities_password_hash']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] How a user proves who they are. N identities → 1 user (email+password, Google, future
Apple/Microsoft/tenant OIDC). Adding a provider = new enum value + adapter; users unchanged.
'''
}

Table auth_sessions {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  user_id bigint [not null, ref: > users.id]
  active_tenant_id bigint [not null, note: 'Tenant context for this session; switching tenants updates this']
  refresh_token_hash bytea [not null, note: 'SHA-256 of opaque rotating refresh token']
  user_agent text
  ip_address inet
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  last_used_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  expires_at timestamptz [not null]
  revoked_at timestamptz

  indexes {
    refresh_token_hash [unique, name: 'uq_auth_sessions_refresh_token_hash']
    user_id [name: 'ix_auth_sessions_user']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Refresh-token session (access tokens are short-lived JWTs carrying sub, sid, tid, ver).
Composite FK to tenant_memberships ensures the active tenant is one the user belongs to.
'''
}

Table action_tokens {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  purpose action_token_purpose [not null, note: 'email_verification | password_reset | tenant_invitation']
  user_id bigint [ref: > users.id, note: 'Required for account verification/reset; NULL for invitations addressed to email']
  tenant_id bigint [ref: > tenants.id, note: 'Only for tenant_invitation']
  email citext [note: 'Recipient email for tenant_invitation']
  role_id bigint [ref: > roles.id, note: 'Role granted when accepting invitation']
  role_scope role_scope [note: 'Always tenant for invitation; used in composite FK']
  token_hash bytea [not null]
  issued_by_user_id bigint [ref: > users.id, note: 'Inviter; NULL for password reset/verification']
  consumed_by_user_id bigint [ref: > users.id, note: 'Actual member who accepted invitation']
  expires_at timestamptz [not null]
  consumed_at timestamptz
  revoked_at timestamptz
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    token_hash [unique, name: 'uq_action_tokens_hash']
    (user_id, purpose) [name: 'ix_action_tokens_user_purpose']
    (tenant_id, email, purpose) [name: 'ix_action_tokens_invite_lookup']
  }

  checks {
    `(purpose = 'tenant_invitation' AND user_id IS NULL AND tenant_id IS NOT NULL AND email IS NOT NULL AND role_id IS NOT NULL AND role_scope = 'tenant' AND issued_by_user_id IS NOT NULL) OR (purpose <> 'tenant_invitation' AND user_id IS NOT NULL AND tenant_id IS NULL AND email IS NULL AND role_id IS NULL AND role_scope IS NULL AND issued_by_user_id IS NULL)` [name: 'ck_action_tokens_purpose_shape']
    `consumed_at IS NULL OR consumed_at >= created_at` [name: 'ck_action_tokens_consumption']
    `consumed_at IS NULL OR revoked_at IS NULL` [name: 'ck_action_tokens_final_state']
    `consumed_by_user_id IS NULL OR (purpose = 'tenant_invitation' AND consumed_at IS NOT NULL)` [name: 'ck_action_tokens_acceptor']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1 account / P4 invitations] Shared single-use token lifecycle: verification, reset, and tenant invitation.
Never store plaintext tokens. Enforce expiration, email-bound acceptance, matching role tenant,
active inviter permission, and single-use CAS during consumption. Consumption is audited here.
Purpose-specific CHECK prevents nullable columns becoming an unstructured EAV model.
'''
}

Table roles {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  tenant_id bigint [ref: > tenants.id, note: 'NULL = system role (seeded). Set = tenant custom role (P4)']
  code text [not null, note: 'learner, teacher, content_manager, tenant_admin, platform_admin, platform_support']
  name text [not null]
  scope role_scope [not null]
  description text
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, code) [unique, name: 'uq_roles_tenant_code', note: 'PG15+: NULLS NOT DISTINCT; on PG14 add partial unique (code) WHERE tenant_id IS NULL']
    (id, scope) [unique, name: 'uq_roles_id_scope', note: 'Target of scope-checked composite FKs']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] RBAC role = named bundle of permissions. Roles never appear as columns on business
tables. Seeded P1: learner; content_manager (granted inside the PLATFORM tenant to the
Engrisk content team); platform_admin, platform_support (platform scope).
Seeded P4: teacher, tenant_admin. Tenant-defined roles are a P4 extension (tenant_id set).
'''
}

Table permissions {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  code text [not null, unique, note: 'resource.action, e.g. attempt.create, content.publish, member.manage']
  scope role_scope [not null]
  description text

  indexes {
    (id, scope) [unique, name: 'uq_permissions_id_scope', note: 'Composite scope FK target']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Permission catalog, seeded from code. Checked by FastAPI dependencies, never by role name.
Content keys (tenant scope; effective only in the session's active tenant):
content.author · content.import · content.review · content.publish (platform tenant, public) ·
content.publish_tenant · content.review_tenant · submission.create.
Service rules: nobody decides their own submission; content.publish never bypasses review
for community provenance.
'''
}

Table role_permissions {
  role_id bigint [not null, ref: > roles.id]
  permission_id bigint [not null, ref: > permissions.id]
  role_scope role_scope [not null, note: 'Enforced to equal BOTH role and permission scope by composite FKs']

  indexes {
    (role_id, permission_id) [pk]
  }

  Note: '[P1] Role ↔ permission. Composite FK scope guards enforce matching role/permission scope in PostgreSQL; no seed-only security invariant.'
}

Table role_assignments {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  role_id bigint [not null]
  role_scope role_scope [not null]
  user_id bigint [ref: > users.id, note: 'Target for platform-scoped role']
  membership_id bigint [ref: > tenant_memberships.id, note: 'Target for tenant-scoped role']
  granted_by_user_id bigint [ref: > users.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (user_id, role_id) [name: 'ix_role_assignments_platform_lookup', note: 'Partial UNIQUE WHERE role_scope = platform']
    (membership_id, role_id) [name: 'ix_role_assignments_membership_lookup', note: 'Partial UNIQUE WHERE role_scope = tenant']
    (role_id, role_scope) [name: 'ix_role_assignments_role']
  }

  checks {
    `(role_scope = 'platform' AND user_id IS NOT NULL AND membership_id IS NULL) OR (role_scope = 'tenant' AND membership_id IS NOT NULL AND user_id IS NULL)` [name: 'ck_role_assignments_target']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] One role assignment model for platform staff and tenant members.
Composite FK (role_id, role_scope) => roles (id, scope) disallows scope mismatch.
For tenant custom roles, validate roles.tenant_id = membership.tenant_id, or roles.tenant_id IS NULL,
under transaction/trigger before granting. CHECK and partial UNIQUE preserve assignment integrity.
'''
}


// =============================================================================
// 2. TENANCY
// =============================================================================

Table tenants {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  kind tenant_kind [not null]
  status tenant_status [not null, default: 'active']
  slug text [not null, unique, note: 'URL-safe; platform tenant = engrisk']
  name text [not null]
  default_locale text [not null, default: 'vi']
  logo_asset_id uuid [note: 'media_assets(purpose = branding) of this tenant']
  settings jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: '{"branding":{"display_name","accent_color","support_email"}, "content_policy":{"requires_review":true}}. Read as one blob, never queried']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  Note: '''
[P1 seeded / P4 self-serve] Organization boundary. Phase 1 has exactly one row (platform).
settings holds presentation (HeroUI --accent mapping) and tenant policies such as
"teacher content requires review". Custom domains (P4) → future tenant_domains table.
'''
}

Table tenant_memberships {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  tenant_id bigint [not null, ref: > tenants.id]
  user_id bigint [not null, ref: > users.id]
  status membership_status [not null, default: 'active']
  permissions_version integer [not null, default: 1, note: 'Bumped on role assignment/status change or when a granted role changes; part of the access-token ver claim']
  joined_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, user_id) [unique, name: 'uq_tenant_memberships_tenant_user', note: 'Target of all learner-data composite FKs']
    user_id [name: 'ix_tenant_memberships_user', note: 'Tenant switcher: list my tenants']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] A user belongs to N tenants. Signup (and guest creation) auto-creates a membership in the
platform tenant with role learner. Never hard-deleted (status = left) so history keeps a parent.
'''
}


Table tenant_entitlements {
  tenant_id bigint [not null, ref: > tenants.id]
  feature_key text [not null, note: 'Code registry: ai_tutor, writing_ai_feedback, speaking_ai_feedback, material_upload, question_generation, platform_library, custom_branding']
  is_enabled boolean [not null, default: true]
  limits jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: 'e.g. {"ai_requests_per_user_per_day": 30}']
  source text [not null, default: 'plan', note: 'plan | override | trial']
  valid_until timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, feature_key) [pk]
  }

  Note: '''
[P1 seeded for platform tenant] Effective feature switches per tenant. Usage is derived from
jobs/ai_runs. Plans/billing stay in code until monetization (future plans + subscriptions).
'''
}


// =============================================================================
// 3. MEDIA (object storage) & SOURCE MATERIALS
// =============================================================================

Table media_assets {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  tenant_id bigint [not null, ref: > tenants.id]
  owner_user_id bigint [ref: > users.id, note: 'Uploader; NULL for system-generated files']
  kind asset_kind [not null]
  purpose asset_purpose [not null]
  status asset_status [not null, default: 'pending_upload']
  storage_key text [not null, note: 'Master object key (R2/MinIO, S3 API). Never exposed; served via short-lived signed URLs after authz']
  original_filename text [note: 'Sanitized client file name (display only, never part of the key)']
  mime_type text [not null]
  byte_size bigint
  sha256 bytea [note: 'Integrity + dedup']
  duration_ms integer [note: 'Audio/video only']
  metadata jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: 'System-observed facts: {width, height, page_count, scan, audio:{sample_rate_hz, channels, loudness_lufs, true_peak_dbtp, silence_head_ms, clipping_samples}}. Audio QC publish gates read this']
  upload jsonb [note: 'In-flight upload only: {strategy: single|multipart, multipart_upload_id, part_size_bytes, part_count, expected_byte_size, expected_sha256, expected_mime, context, expires_at}; cleared when available']
  variants jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: 'Renditions: {"aac_96k": {key, mime_type, byte_size, duration_ms}, "webp_640": {...}}']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  deleted_at timestamptz

  indexes {
    storage_key [unique, name: 'uq_media_assets_storage_key']
    (tenant_id, id) [unique, name: 'uq_media_assets_tenant_id', note: 'Composite FK target']
    (tenant_id, owner_user_id, purpose) [name: 'ix_media_assets_owner']
    (tenant_id, sha256) [name: 'ix_media_assets_digest', note: 'Optional dedup candidate lookup; NOT globally unique because rights/purposes differ']
    (status, updated_at) [name: 'ix_media_assets_cleanup', note: 'Partial: WHERE status IN (pending_upload, processing, quarantined) — cleanup sweeper']
  }

  checks {
    `duration_ms IS NULL OR duration_ms > 0` [name: 'ck_media_assets_duration']
    `byte_size IS NULL OR byte_size >= 0` [name: 'ck_media_assets_size']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Every binary file (audio, images, PDFs, recordings, logos, import packages/reports,
delivery assets). Access is decided by the referencing entity (content version link,
source material, response, tenant logo), never by the asset alone. Upload: row (pending_upload)
→ presigned PUT/multipart → processing (scan/probe/transcode) → available | quarantined.
Measured audio QC lives in metadata because it is a property of the immutable file.
Published / historically served media cannot be hard-deleted even if a tenant archives it;
implement reference-aware retention and short-lived signed access per allowed context.
'''
}

Table source_materials {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  tenant_id bigint [not null, ref: > tenants.id]
  owner_user_id bigint [not null]
  asset_id uuid [not null]
  title text [not null]
  rights_basis rights_basis [not null]
  rights_confirmed_at timestamptz [not null, note: 'Learner confirmed they may use this material']
  status material_status [not null, default: 'uploaded']
  failure_reason text
  extracted_text text [note: 'Text extracted for generation (TOAST-compressed). Never shown to other users']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  deleted_at timestamptz

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, id) [unique, name: 'uq_source_materials_tenant_id']
    (tenant_id, owner_user_id, created_at) [name: 'ix_source_materials_owner']
  }

  Note: '''
[P3] A learning document uploaded to generate practice. Always private to its owner.
Lifecycle: uploaded → processing → ready | failed | rejected. Content generated from it starts
as private drafts (content_item_versions.source_material_id) and never feeds the public bank
automatically. rights_basis = personal_study_only can never back tenant/public content.
Specialized (not a content item) because it has its own rights + extraction lifecycle.
'''
}

// =============================================================================
// 4. REFERENCE DATA (global, code-seeded)
// =============================================================================

Table exam_types {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  code text [not null, unique, note: 'toeic_lr, ielts_academic, ielts_general; later toeic_sw, cambridge_*']
  name text [not null, note: 'English fallback; localized names served from the code i18n catalog keyed by code']
  scoring_policy_key text [not null, note: 'Default code-defined scorer, e.g. toeic_lr_v1, ielts_v1; pinned per version at publish']
  score_scale jsonb [not null, note: 'UI bounds for goals: {"min":10,"max":990,"step":5} or {"min":0,"max":9,"step":0.5}']
  is_active boolean [not null, default: true]

  Note: '''
[P1] Global catalog of standardized test formats — a genuinely specific domain concept (score
scale + scorer). A new format = new row + scorer + section schema_keys; no new tables.
'''
}

Table skills {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  code text [not null, unique, note: 'e.g. reading.inference, grammar.verb_tense, toeic.part2.question_response']
  name text [not null, note: 'English fallback; localized via code i18n catalog']
  area skill_area [note: 'NULL for cross-area skills like grammar/vocabulary; specific area when the competency is modality-specific']
  exam_type_id bigint [ref: > exam_types.id, note: 'NULL = cross-exam skill (grammar, vocabulary, inference)']
  parent_id bigint [ref: > skills.id]
  position smallint [not null, default: 0]
  is_active boolean [not null, default: true]

  indexes {
    (area, exam_type_id) [name: 'ix_skills_area_exam_type']
    parent_id [name: 'ix_skills_parent']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Global skill taxonomy (tree). No dependency on mutable section labels or JSONB keys.
Area can be NULL for a truly cross-area skill. Validate no parent cycles. A skill is assigned
to a content version; a syllabus/part is a content item rather than a skill.
'''
}

// =============================================================================
// 5. CONTENT GRAPH (Core V2: versioned content graph)
// =============================================================================

Table content_items {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  tenant_id bigint [not null, ref: > tenants.id]
  kind text [not null, note: 'Code registry of broad structural kinds: collection | exam | section | block | stimulus | question; later course | module | lesson | flashcard_deck. Immutable']
  exam_type_id bigint [ref: > exam_types.id, note: 'Required for kind = exam. NULL for reusable / cross-format components']
  slug text [note: 'Stable URL key; required for catalog roots, NULL for internal components']
  visibility content_visibility [not null, default: 'tenant']
  access_tier access_tier [not null, default: 'registered']
  provenance content_provenance [note: 'Catalog trust label for publishable roots; set by the service from tenant kind + creator role; immutable after first publish. NULL for components']
  owner_user_id bigint [note: 'Private owner (personal practice, community draft); NULL for tenant/platform-authored content']
  current_published_version_id uuid [note: 'Version served to NEW attempts/placements; atomically promoted at publish']
  created_by_user_id bigint [ref: > users.id]
  archived_at timestamptz [note: 'Hidden from catalog and pickers; history intact']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, id) [unique, name: 'uq_content_items_tenant_id']
    (tenant_id, kind, slug) [unique, name: 'uq_content_items_tenant_kind_slug', note: 'Partial: WHERE slug IS NOT NULL']
    (tenant_id, kind, exam_type_id, visibility) [name: 'ix_content_items_catalog', note: 'Partial: WHERE archived_at IS NULL AND current_published_version_id IS NOT NULL']
    (tenant_id, owner_user_id) [name: 'ix_content_items_owner', note: 'Partial: WHERE owner_user_id IS NOT NULL']
    (tenant_id, provenance) [name: 'ix_content_items_provenance', note: 'Partial: WHERE provenance IS NOT NULL — catalog sections "Từ cộng đồng" / tenant shelf']
  }

  checks {
    `visibility <> 'private' OR owner_user_id IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_content_items_private_owner']
    `kind <> 'exam' OR exam_type_id IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_content_items_exam_type']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] One logical object, stable across versions and reused in many parent trees (NO parent_id).
Operational state (visibility, access tier, provenance, archival, published pointer) lives here;
everything historical lives in versions. Visibility public only in the platform tenant;
engrisk_original/community only in the platform tenant, tenant_authored only in organizations
(service rules). Community drafts are private + owner = contributor until approved.
Catalog listing = items ⋈ current published version (1:1 PK join); counters computed from aggregate views or on-demand cached projections.
'''
}

Table content_item_versions {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  tenant_id bigint [not null]
  item_id uuid [not null]
  version_no integer [not null]
  status version_status [not null, default: 'draft']
  schema_key text [not null, note: 'Registry contract "<kind>.<variant>": exam.full_mock | exam.section_test | exam.practice_set | exam.personal_practice | section.timed | section.audio_paced | block.group | stimulus.passage | stimulus.audio | stimulus.image | stimulus.audio_image | question.single_choice | question.multiple_choice | question.fill_blank | question.matching | question.ordering | question.short_answer | question.essay | question.speaking | collection.shelf; later lesson.*, course.*. Prefix must equal item kind']
  schema_version integer [not null, default: 1, note: 'Payload contract version; validated by Pydantic/JSON Schema']
  title text
  body jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: 'Learner-visible document only. Question: {stem, options[{key,text}], blanks, word_limit, prep_seconds}. Passage: {documents:[{title, kind, blocks:[{type,label,text}]}]}. Image: {alt}. Exam: {description}. Never answers or transcripts']
  settings jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: 'Versioned behaviour. Exam: {time_limit_seconds, presentation:{cover:{motif,tint,label}}}. Section: {key:"L", skill_area, time_limit_seconds, delivery:"audio_paced"|"timed", check_seconds, rules:{audio_replay, annotations}, directions}']
  rollup jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: 'Computed at publish for composite versions, immutable: {question_count, max_points, duration_seconds, section_keys[]}. Display only, never filtered']
  difficulty smallint [note: '1..5 (UI 1–2 Easy, 3 Medium, 4–5 Hard); questions and catalog roots']
  default_points numeric(7,2) [note: 'Scorable leaves; a placement may override']
  scoring_policy_key text [note: 'Pinned scorer for assessment roots, copied from exam_types at publish']
  origin content_origin [not null, default: 'human']
  ai_run_id bigint [ref: > ai_runs.id, note: 'Generation run when origin = ai_generated']
  source_material_id uuid [note: 'Learner upload this version was generated from']
  based_on_version_id uuid [note: 'Previous version of the SAME logical item; composite FK guarantees lineage. Cross-item copies create a new item and record provenance separately.']
  change_note text [note: 'Release notes: Studio history + "Có gì mới" for learners']
  publish_at timestamptz [note: 'Scheduled publish time (status = scheduled)']
  published_at timestamptz
  published_by_user_id bigint [ref: > users.id, note: 'Human who published; for ai_generated content this is the approving reviewer']
  created_by_user_id bigint [ref: > users.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`, note: 'Bumped by any draft change incl. relations, asset links, timelines, answer specs → ETag']

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, id) [unique, name: 'uq_content_item_versions_tenant_id']
    (item_id, id) [unique, name: 'uq_content_item_versions_item_id', note: 'Target of same-item composite FKs']
    (item_id, version_no) [unique, name: 'uq_content_item_versions_number']
    (item_id, status) [name: 'ix_content_item_versions_status', note: 'Add partial UNIQUE (item_id) WHERE status = draft — one mutable draft per item']
    (tenant_id, schema_key, status, difficulty) [name: 'ix_content_item_versions_bank', note: 'Question bank / picker filters']
    (status, publish_at) [name: 'ix_content_item_versions_scheduled', note: 'Partial: WHERE status = scheduled — publish scheduler']
    source_material_id [name: 'ix_content_item_versions_source_material', note: 'Partial: WHERE source_material_id IS NOT NULL']
  }

  checks {
    `version_no > 0` [name: 'ck_content_item_versions_number']
    `difficulty IS NULL OR difficulty BETWEEN 1 AND 5` [name: 'ck_content_item_versions_difficulty']
    `default_points IS NULL OR default_points >= 0` [name: 'ck_content_item_versions_points']
    `origin <> 'ai_generated' OR ai_run_id IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_content_item_versions_ai_provenance']
    `status <> 'scheduled' OR publish_at IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_content_item_versions_scheduled_at']
    `status NOT IN ('published','retired') OR published_at IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_content_item_versions_published_at']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Immutable-after-publish version of any content item. One table for exams, sections,
groups, stimuli and all question types (type-specific shape = schema_key-typed body/settings,
not sub-tables or EAV). Editing published content creates a new version; parents and attempts
pinning the old version are unaffected. Triggers (outside DBML): reject changes to semantic fields of published/retired versions and all edits/deletes
of their relations, asset links, timelines and answer specs; permit only the audited
published → retired lifecycle transition (without changing content);
schema_key prefix = item kind. One mutable draft per item; atomic publish validates and freezes
the full assessment graph (all descendants pinned to published versions). AI-generated versions need a human publisher
(published_by_user_id); private personal-practice content is approved by its owner.
'''
}

Table content_item_relations {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  tenant_id bigint [not null, note: 'Tenant of the parent version. The child may be a granted/public item of another tenant']
  parent_version_id uuid [not null]
  child_item_id uuid [not null, ref: > content_items.id]
  child_version_id uuid [note: 'Exact child version when binding_mode = pinned; NULL when latest_published']
  binding_mode binding_mode [not null, default: 'pinned']
  slot text [not null, default: 'content', note: 'Registry: content (ordered structural/scorable children) | stimulus (shared material of a block) | instructions (non-scorable directions/examples)']
  position integer [not null, note: 'Order inside (parent_version_id, slot). Global question numbers are compiled into the delivery manifest']
  points_override numeric(7,2) [note: 'Placement-specific marks; NULL = child default_points']
  settings jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: 'Placement-only config, e.g. {"page_break":true,"optional":false}. Never child content or keys']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (parent_version_id, slot, position) [unique, name: 'uq_content_item_relations_order']
    (tenant_id, parent_version_id) [name: 'ix_content_item_relations_parent']
    child_item_id [name: 'ix_content_item_relations_usage', note: 'Where is this item used?']
    child_version_id [name: 'ix_content_item_relations_child_version']
  }

  checks {
    `position >= 0` [name: 'ck_content_item_relations_position']
    `points_override IS NULL OR points_override >= 0` [name: 'ck_content_item_relations_points']
    `(binding_mode = 'pinned') = (child_version_id IS NOT NULL)` [name: 'ck_content_item_relations_binding']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Placements: ordered, versioned composition with reusable children (replaces
exam_revision_items, questions.question_group_id and exam_revisions.sections). Parent is
always an exact version and is frozen with it. Publish validation: no cycles, allowed kind
transitions (registry), every descendant of an assessment root pinned + published, compatible
exam types, grants for cross-tenant children, scoring/answer coverage, media status.
A new draft root version clones the previous version's relations (copy-on-write).
Do not deduplicate a child across placements: relation.id identifies each occurrence;
unique (parent_version_id, slot, position) is the ordering invariant. A published root must
resolve every dynamic descendant to pinned versions before creating its manifest.
'''
}

Table content_version_assets {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  tenant_id bigint [not null]
  content_version_id uuid [not null]
  asset_id uuid [not null]
  role text [not null, note: 'Registry: cover | image | audio | video | document. audio on a section version = continuous section track; on a stimulus = group clip']
  position integer [not null, default: 0]
  settings jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: 'Learner-visible presentation: {caption, alt, crop, document_index}. Never storage keys or protected text']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (content_version_id, role, position) [unique, name: 'uq_content_version_assets_position']
    asset_id [name: 'ix_content_version_assets_asset', note: 'Media authorization: which versions expose this asset?']
  }

  checks {
    `position >= 0` [name: 'ck_content_version_assets_position']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Media placed in a content version (replaces question_groups.audio/image_asset_id,
exams.cover_asset_id and revision_audio_tracks.asset_id). One asset may be linked by many
versions; storage metadata stays in media_assets. Same tenant as the version (composite FK).
'''
}

Table content_media_timelines {
  content_version_asset_id uuid [pk, note: 'One timeline per audio/video placement']
  cues jsonb [not null, default: `'[]'::jsonb`, note: 'PROTECTED. [{relation_path:[relation_uuid,...], start_ms, end_ms, confidence, source}] — path resolves one exact occurrence, even if a question repeats within the same exam. Validate against pinned tree at publish']
  transcript_segments jsonb [not null, default: `'[]'::jsonb`, note: 'PROTECTED. [{start_ms?, end_ms?, speaker:"M1"|"W1"|"N", accent:"us"|"uk"|"au"|"ca", text, item_ids:[]}] — English; times optional until aligned']
  ai_run_id bigint [ref: > ai_runs.id, note: 'Last forced-alignment / synthesis run']
  aligned_at timestamptz
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  Note: '''
[P1] Protected timing layer of a media placement: section-track cue maps (TOEIC L, IELTS
Listening parts) and timed transcripts of group clips, in one model (replaces
revision_audio_tracks.cues/script_segments and question_groups.transcript). Separate from
content_version_assets.settings so delivery queries never read protected text. Copy-on-write
with its version; immutable once the version is published. QC thresholds are publish gates
evaluated against media_assets.metadata.audio.
'''
}

Table content_answer_specs {
  question_version_id uuid [pk, ref: > content_item_versions.id]
  answer_key jsonb [note: 'Objective grading, server-only. {"type":"single_choice","choice":"B"} | {"type":"fill_blank","accept":[...]} | {"type":"matching","matches":{...}}. NULL for essay/speaking']
  rubric_key text [note: 'Versioned evaluator rubric for essay/speaking, e.g. ielts_writing_task2_v1']
  explanation jsonb [note: 'Disclosed in review only: {"texts":{"vi":"…","en":"…"}, "evidence":{"stimulus_item_id":…, "document_index":0, "start":120, "end":168, "quote":"…"}}']
  grading_config jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: 'Partial credit, case sensitivity, accepted variants policy']

  checks {
    `answer_key IS NOT NULL OR rubric_key IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_content_answer_specs_grading']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] PROTECTED grading data of a question version, physically outside learner-visible body.
Read only by grading/review/authoring code paths (restricted role). Only question versions
have specs (publish validator); objective schemas require answer_key, essay/speaking rubric_key.
'''
}

Table content_version_skills {
  content_version_id uuid [not null, ref: > content_item_versions.id]
  skill_id bigint [not null, ref: > skills.id]
  is_primary boolean [not null, default: false]

  indexes {
    (content_version_id, skill_id) [pk]
    skill_id [name: 'ix_content_version_skills_skill']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Skill tags on any version: question versions (per-skill results, weak skills, adaptive
targeting) and catalog roots (skill filter = root skills of an area, replacing exams.skill_focus).
At most one primary per version (partial UNIQUE (content_version_id) WHERE is_primary).
Belongs to the exact version for reproducible history.
'''
}


// =============================================================================
// 6. CONTENT ECOSYSTEM (sharing, attribution, feedback, read models)
// =============================================================================

Table content_access_grants {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  item_id uuid [not null, ref: > content_items.id, note: 'Granted root (exam, course, collection)']
  grantee_tenant_id bigint [not null, ref: > tenants.id]
  allowed_actions text[] [not null, default: `ARRAY['consume']::text[]`, note: 'Registry values: consume (serve/attempt) | embed (place into a new authored tree). Always validate both permissions at publish and read.']
  granted_by_user_id bigint [ref: > users.id]
  starts_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  ends_at timestamptz
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (item_id, grantee_tenant_id) [unique, name: 'uq_content_access_grants_item_tenant']
    grantee_tenant_id [name: 'ix_content_access_grants_grantee']
  }

  checks {
    `ends_at IS NULL OR ends_at > starts_at` [name: 'ck_content_access_grants_window']
    `cardinality(allowed_actions) > 0` [name: 'ck_content_access_grants_actions']
  }

  Note: '''
[P4] Explicit cross-tenant sharing of a root item (replaces exam_licenses): grantee members may
consume or embed it ONLY according to allowed_actions; the owner keeps editing. Grant checks
are required at reference creation, publish, and delivery; history remains reviewable under a
separately defined post-expiry policy. Coarse alternative:
tenant_entitlements.platform_library = all public platform content.
'''
}

Table content_credits {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  item_id uuid [not null, ref: > content_items.id]
  user_id bigint [ref: > users.id, note: 'NULL for external people (e.g. a hired narrator)']
  display_name text [note: 'Public name; required when user_id IS NULL']
  role credit_role [not null]
  position smallint [not null, default: 0]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (item_id, user_id, role) [unique, name: 'uq_content_credits_person_role', note: 'Partial: WHERE user_id IS NOT NULL']
    user_id [name: 'ix_content_credits_user', note: 'Contributor profile: published work']
  }

  checks {
    `user_id IS NOT NULL OR display_name IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_content_credits_identity']
  }

  Note: '''
[P3] Public attribution on catalog cards, intro and results. Mandatory for provenance =
community and for CC BY 4.0. Item-level credit roster is mutable; the publisher should
snapshot attribution in the immutable manifest for historical presentation/licensing.
'''
}

Table content_ratings {
  item_id uuid [not null, ref: > content_items.id]
  user_id bigint [not null]
  tenant_id bigint [not null, note: 'Tenant context the learner rated in (membership)']
  content_version_id uuid [not null, note: 'Version the learner actually took (same item, composite FK)']
  rating smallint [not null]
  issue_tags text[] [note: 'Optional low-rating reasons: wrong_key | unclear_audio | typo | too_easy | too_hard']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (item_id, user_id) [pk]
  }

  checks {
    `rating BETWEEN 1 AND 5` [name: 'ck_content_ratings_range']
  }

  Note: '''
[P3] One 1–5 rating per learner per root item (upsert) after a completed attempt (service rule).
Aggregates come from content_ratings (optional Redis/materialized-view cache); shown when ≥ 10 ratings.
'''
}

Table content_reports {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  tenant_id bigint [not null, ref: > tenants.id, note: 'Content-owner tenant (routes the Studio todo)']
  reporter_user_id bigint [not null]
  reporter_tenant_id bigint [not null, note: 'Tenant context of the reporter (platform content may be reported from an org)']
  kind text [not null, note: 'question_error | copyright | inappropriate | other']
  root_item_id uuid [not null, ref: > content_items.id, note: 'Catalog/assessment root that the learner encountered']
  reported_version_id uuid [ref: > content_item_versions.id, note: 'Exact offending node version (can be a child question, not necessarily a version of root_item_id)']
  attempt_id bigint [ref: > attempts.id, note: 'PROTECTED. Platform support only; owner tenant never sees learner answers']
  issue_tags text[]
  message text
  status report_status [not null, default: 'open']
  resolved_by_user_id bigint [ref: > users.id]
  resolution_note text
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, status, created_at) [name: 'ix_content_reports_queue']
    (reporter_user_id, created_at) [name: 'ix_content_reports_reporter', note: 'Rate limiting']
    root_item_id [name: 'ix_content_reports_root_item']
    reported_version_id [name: 'ix_content_reports_version']
  }

  checks {
    `kind IN ('question_error','copyright','inappropriate','other')` [name: 'ck_content_reports_kind']
    `status = 'open' OR resolved_by_user_id IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_content_reports_resolution']
  }

  Note: '[P3] Learner reports of content problems (copyright takedown, wrong key, unsafe). Registered users only. Validate that reported_version_id is present in the exact served root manifest; not the same logical item as root_item_id.'
}


// =============================================================================
// 7. CONTENT WORKFLOW (import · submissions · moderation · comments)
// =============================================================================

Table content_imports {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  tenant_id bigint [not null, ref: > tenants.id]
  created_by_user_id bigint [not null]
  package_asset_id uuid [not null, note: 'media_assets(purpose = import_package), ZIP ≤ 2 GB']
  report_asset_id uuid [note: 'media_assets(purpose = import_report), full CSV issues report']
  manifest_format text [not null, note: 'xlsx | csv | json']
  manifest_version text [not null, note: 'Template version, e.g. engrisk-import/1.2']
  exam_type_id bigint [not null, ref: > exam_types.id]
  status import_status [not null, default: 'uploaded']
  rights_basis rights_basis [not null]
  rights_confirmed_at timestamptz [not null]
  summary jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: '{"rows_total":200, "rows_ok":193, "rows_error":7, "rows_warning":12, "assets_matched":54, "assets_missing":2, "assets_unused":1}']
  issues jsonb [not null, default: `'[]'::jsonb`, note: 'First 500: [{row, column, code, severity:"error"|"warning", message, hint}]; complete list in report_asset_id']
  file_matches jsonb [not null, default: `'[]'::jsonb`, note: 'First 500: [{path, kind, matched_to, status: matched|missing|unused}]']
  root_item_id uuid [note: 'Draft root created (or updated with a new draft version) on completion']
  root_version_id uuid
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  started_at timestamptz
  finished_at timestamptz

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, created_at) [name: 'ix_content_imports_tenant']
  }

  checks {
    `rights_basis <> 'personal_study_only'` [name: 'ck_content_imports_rights']
    `status <> 'completed' OR root_version_id IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_content_imports_result']
    `(root_item_id IS NULL) = (root_version_id IS NULL)` [name: 'ck_content_imports_root_pair']
  }

  Note: '''
[P3] Bulk import of a standard package into a DRAFT root version. Business record with legal
rights confirmation; the async work runs as jobs (kind import_validation, target content_import).
Lifecycle: uploaded → validating → validated | failed → completed. Validation never writes
content; "Tạo bản nháp" does, in one transaction (origin = imported).
'''
}

Table content_submissions {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  tenant_id bigint [not null, note: 'Target (owning) tenant where the content will be published']
  item_id uuid [not null]
  content_version_id uuid [not null, note: 'Version frozen at submit (status in_review while active)']
  submitter_user_id bigint [not null]
  status submission_status [not null, default: 'submitted']
  round smallint [not null, default: 1, note: '+1 on each resubmission after changes_requested']
  license contribution_license [note: 'Required for provenance = community; NULL for tenant-internal submissions']
  rights_basis rights_basis [not null, default: 'own_work']
  rights_confirmed_at timestamptz [not null, note: 'Contributor confirmed originality + licence at submit']
  message_to_reviewer text
  auto_checks jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: 'Snapshot of automated gate results: {"schema":"pass", "keys_complete":"pass", "audio_qc":"pass", "originality":{"status":"pass","max_similarity":0.12}, "safety":"pass"}']
  assigned_reviewer_user_id bigint [ref: > users.id]
  sla_due_at timestamptz [note: 'submitted_at + 5 business days (community) / 2 (tenant)']
  appeal_of_submission_id bigint [ref: > content_submissions.id, note: 'Appeal of a rejected submission (one appeal allowed)']
  submitted_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  decided_at timestamptz
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, id) [unique, name: 'uq_content_submissions_tenant_id']
    item_id [name: 'ix_content_submissions_active', note: 'Implement as partial UNIQUE (item_id) WHERE status IN (submitted, in_review, changes_requested): one active submission per item']
    (tenant_id, status, sla_due_at) [name: 'ix_content_submissions_queue', note: 'Moderation queue ordered by SLA']
    (submitter_user_id, status) [name: 'ix_content_submissions_submitter', note: '"Đóng góp của tôi"']
    (assigned_reviewer_user_id, status) [name: 'ix_content_submissions_reviewer']
  }

  checks {
    `status NOT IN ('approved','rejected') OR decided_at IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_content_submissions_decided']
    `assigned_reviewer_user_id IS NULL OR assigned_reviewer_user_id <> submitter_user_id` [name: 'ck_content_submissions_no_self_review']
    `rights_basis <> 'personal_study_only'` [name: 'ck_content_submissions_rights']
    `round >= 1` [name: 'ck_content_submissions_round']
  }

  Note: '''
[P3] Request to publish one version through review: community contributions into the platform
tenant, and P4 teacher drafts when tenants.settings.content_policy.requires_review. Drafts are
draft versions, not submissions. approve = version published/scheduled + item visibility public
(community) + content_credits rows.
'''
}


Table content_comments {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  tenant_id bigint [not null]
  content_version_id uuid [not null, note: 'Anchor: exact version (root, section, stimulus or question)']
  submission_id bigint [note: 'Set for moderation threads']
  submission_round smallint [note: 'content_submissions.round at creation; resubmit requires previous-round comments resolved']
  parent_comment_id bigint [ref: > content_comments.id, note: 'Thread reply']
  kind comment_kind [not null, default: 'comment']
  author_user_id bigint [ref: > users.id, note: 'NULL for system/AI flags']
  ai_run_id bigint [ref: > ai_runs.id, note: 'Quality-check run that raised a flag']
  code text [note: 'Flag code, e.g. ambiguous_key, missing_alt, cue_gap']
  decision review_decision [note: 'Required for kind=review_decision; moderator action']
  decision_checklist jsonb [note: 'Versioned review checklist, required for decision event']
  decision_reason_code text [note: 'Required for rejected/changes-requested decisions']
  severity text [not null, default: 'info', note: 'info | warning | blocking (blocking flags fail the publish validator)']
  anchor jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: '{"field":"stem"|"options"|"answer_key"|"explanation"|"stimulus"|"image_alt"|"audio"|"transcript"|"metadata", "media_ms":1200, "option_key":"B"}']
  body text [not null]
  resolved_at timestamptz
  resolved_by_user_id bigint [ref: > users.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (content_version_id, resolved_at) [name: 'ix_content_comments_version_open']
    (submission_id, submission_round, resolved_at) [name: 'ix_content_comments_submission_open', note: 'Partial: WHERE submission_id IS NOT NULL']
    (submission_id, submission_round) [name: 'ix_content_comments_decision_round_lookup', note: 'Partial UNIQUE WHERE kind = review_decision: at most one decision per round']
  }

  checks {
    `kind = 'flag' OR author_user_id IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_content_comments_author']
    `kind <> 'flag' OR code IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_content_comments_flag_code']
    `(kind = 'review_decision') = (decision IS NOT NULL)` [name: 'ck_content_comments_decision_kind']
    `kind <> 'review_decision' OR (submission_id IS NOT NULL AND parent_comment_id IS NULL AND author_user_id IS NOT NULL AND decision_checklist IS NOT NULL AND (decision = 'approve' OR decision_reason_code IS NOT NULL))` [name: 'ck_content_comments_decision_required']
    `kind = 'review_decision' OR (decision_checklist IS NULL AND decision_reason_code IS NULL)` [name: 'ck_content_comments_decision_fields']
    `(submission_id IS NULL) = (submission_round IS NULL)` [name: 'ck_content_comments_round']
    `severity IN ('info','warning','blocking')` [name: 'ck_content_comments_severity']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1 flags / P3 moderation] One anchored feedback model for authoring (replaces
questions.review_flags JSONB and review_comments): human comments in moderation and Studio,
plus validator/AI quality flags as resolvable rows. A moderator's decision is an immutable
kind=review_decision event (enforced by partial UNIQUE per submission/round), superseding
moderation decision events. Do not mutate decision rows; application must atomically update submission
status and write the event. Flags and decisions are never shown to learners unless authorized.
'''
}

// =============================================================================
// 8. LEARNING RECORDS
// =============================================================================

Table learning_goals {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  tenant_id bigint [not null]
  user_id bigint [not null]
  exam_type_id bigint [not null, ref: > exam_types.id]
  status goal_status [not null, default: 'active']
  self_assessed_level text [note: 'Onboarding answer: new | basic | intermediate | advanced']
  baseline_score numeric(6,2) [note: 'Self-reported previous score (not verified)']
  target_score numeric(6,2) [note: 'Bounds from exam_types.score_scale']
  target_date date
  weekly_study_minutes smallint
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, user_id, exam_type_id) [name: 'ix_learning_goals_user', note: 'Partial unique: WHERE status = active (one active goal per exam type)']
  }

  Note: '[P1] Onboarding output; basis for "recommended next" and goal progress. Registered users only (service rule).'
}

Table attempts {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  tenant_id bigint [not null, note: 'Tenant context the learner practised in']
  user_id bigint [not null]
  content_item_id uuid [ref: > content_items.id, note: 'Root item (exam, lesson quiz…). Denormalized for per-item filters/uniqueness; NULL only for system-composed adaptive practice']
  content_version_id uuid [note: 'Pinned root version (same item, composite FK). NULL only for adaptive practice']
  served_manifest_asset_id uuid [not null, ref: > media_assets.id, note: 'Immutable, learner-visible content manifest for this sitting; pin even for adaptive sessions with no root version']
  mode attempt_mode [not null]
  status attempt_status [not null, default: 'in_progress']
  settings jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: 'Chosen at setup, immutable after start. Practice: {"section_keys":["P5","P7"],"time_limit_seconds":900,"instant_check":true,"audio_replay":true,"transcript":true}. Display prefs {"font":"lg","tone":"cream"} may change']
  resume_state jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: 'UI state only; updated with optimistic locking (resume_revision), never authoritative for grading']
  resume_revision bigint [not null, default: 0, note: 'Server CAS version for cross-device resume writes; clients must supply expected revision']
  sections_state jsonb [not null, default: `'[]'::jsonb`, note: 'Server-owned windows: [{key:"L", opens_at, closes_at, closed_at, close_reason: time|learner|auto}]']
  started_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  deadline_at timestamptz [note: 'Server-authoritative end for timed attempts']
  paused_at timestamptz [note: 'Practice only; resume extends deadline_at by now() - paused_at']
  last_activity_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  submitted_at timestamptz
  submit_reason submit_reason
  completed_at timestamptz
  active_seconds integer [not null, default: 0, note: 'Accumulated time on task (excludes paused practice)']

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, user_id, started_at) [name: 'ix_attempts_history']
    (status, deadline_at) [name: 'ix_attempts_deadline_sweep', note: 'Partial: WHERE status = in_progress AND deadline_at IS NOT NULL']
    content_version_id [name: 'ix_attempts_version']
  }

  checks {
    `mode = 'practice' OR content_version_id IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_attempts_mock_has_version']
    `(content_item_id IS NULL) = (content_version_id IS NULL)` [name: 'ck_attempts_root_pair']
    `(status IN ('submitted','completed')) = (submitted_at IS NOT NULL)` [name: 'ck_attempts_submitted_at']
    `paused_at IS NULL OR mode = 'practice'` [name: 'ck_attempts_pause_practice_only']
    `resume_revision >= 0` [name: 'ck_attempts_resume_revision']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] One learner sitting = historical fact, pinned to an exact root version. Same engine for
practice sets, section tests, full mocks (TOEIC/IELTS) and future lesson quizzes/adaptive
sessions; differences live in version settings and the scoring policy. Composite FK
(content_item_id, content_version_id) guarantees the pair is consistent.
served_manifest_asset_id pins the fully resolved, sanitized delivery snapshot for static and
adaptive practice; the snapshot must be available before the attempt starts.
Guest attempts are ordinary attempts of a guest user. Exam rules are enforced server-side.
Partial UNIQUE for active attempts is defined in companion SQL, not as a global DBML unique.
'''
}

Table attempt_responses {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  attempt_id bigint [not null, ref: > attempts.id]
  question_version_id uuid [not null, ref: > content_item_versions.id, note: 'Exact question version served']
  served_key text [not null, note: 'Occurrence key from immutable served manifest, e.g. serialized relation path; distinguishes repeated placement of the SAME question version']
  section_key text [note: 'Section settings.key it was served in; NULL for adaptive practice']
  position integer [not null, note: 'Served question number (1-based) — historical record']
  max_points numeric(7,2) [not null, note: 'Effective placement points copied at start']
  answer jsonb [note: 'NULL = unanswered. Same shape as the API Answer: {"type":"single_choice","choice":"B"} | {"type":"matching","matches":{"14":"C"}} | {"type":"speaking","duration_ms":…}']
  answer_asset_id uuid [ref: > media_assets.id, note: 'Recording (purpose response_media); single source of truth for speaking answers']
  eliminated text[] [not null, default: `'{}'`, note: 'Option keys struck out by the learner']
  is_flagged boolean [not null, default: false, note: 'Mark for review']
  row_revision bigint [not null, default: 0, note: 'Server-owned optimistic write revision; expected revision required on save, conflict = HTTP 409']
  first_answered_at timestamptz
  last_saved_at timestamptz
  time_spent_ms integer [not null, default: 0]
  is_correct boolean [note: 'Deterministic key grading; NULL for essay/speaking or ungraded']
  points_awarded numeric(7,2) [note: 'Key-graded points, or the current evaluation result']
  graded_at timestamptz [note: 'Also the practice answer lock']

  indexes {
    (attempt_id, position) [unique, name: 'uq_attempt_responses_position']
    (attempt_id, served_key) [unique, name: 'uq_attempt_responses_served_key']
    question_version_id [name: 'ix_attempt_responses_question', note: 'Item analytics (p-value, distractors); group by item via versions']
  }

  checks {
    `max_points >= 0` [name: 'ck_attempt_responses_points']
    `row_revision >= 0` [name: 'ck_attempt_responses_revision']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] One row per SERVED question, created at attempt start (unanswered = answer NULL).
Each row identifies the served OCCURRENCE, not only the question version.
Autosave uses expected row_revision + atomic compare-and-swap and idempotency for retries.
No silent last-write-wins across devices; return conflict and let client merge/retry.
Objective grading writes is_correct/points_awarded; subjective feedback lives in evaluations.
'''
}

Table attempt_annotations {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  attempt_id bigint [not null, ref: > attempts.id]
  content_version_id uuid [not null, ref: > content_item_versions.id, note: 'Exact stimulus version the range belongs to (passage, document, transcript)']
  kind annotation_kind [not null]
  anchor jsonb [not null, note: '{"document_index":0,"start":120,"end":168,"quote":"Rooftops in London…"} — offsets in the rendered plain text of that version']
  body text [note: 'Note text; NULL for plain highlights']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (attempt_id, content_version_id) [name: 'ix_attempt_annotations_attempt']
  }

  Note: '[P1] Highlights and notes made while taking a test, shown again in review. Anchored to an immutable version so offsets stay valid. Private to the learner.'
}

Table evaluations {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  attempt_response_id bigint [not null, ref: > attempt_responses.id]
  evaluator_kind evaluator_kind [not null]
  evaluator_user_id bigint [ref: > users.id, note: 'Teacher for human evaluations']
  job_id uuid [ref: > jobs.id, note: 'Async job producing an AI evaluation']
  ai_run_id bigint [ref: > ai_runs.id, note: 'Run that produced the completed result']
  status evaluation_status [not null, default: 'pending']
  rubric_key text [not null, note: 'Copied from content_answer_specs at evaluation time']
  criteria_scores jsonb [note: 'Keys = API criterion vocabulary, e.g. {"task_response":6.5,"coherence_cohesion":6}']
  estimated_score numeric(5,2) [note: 'AI/teacher band estimate']
  feedback jsonb [note: '{summary, strengths[], improvements[], inline:[{start,end,suggestion,category}], estimated_range:{low,high}, low_confidence_criteria[], transcript?:{text,segments,confidence}}']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  completed_at timestamptz

  indexes {
    (attempt_response_id, created_at) [name: 'ix_evaluations_response', note: 'Partial unique (attempt_response_id) WHERE status = completed — one current evaluation']
  }

  checks {
    `evaluator_kind <> 'ai' OR ai_run_id IS NOT NULL OR (status IN ('pending','failed') AND job_id IS NOT NULL)` [name: 'ck_evaluations_ai_provenance']
    `evaluator_kind <> 'human' OR evaluator_user_id IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_evaluations_human_evaluator']
  }

  Note: '[P2] Subjective assessment of essay/speaking responses, separate from key grading. A teacher evaluation (P4) supersedes the AI one without deleting it; failed evaluations are kept.'
}

Table attempt_scores {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  attempt_id bigint [not null, ref: > attempts.id]
  scope_key text [not null, note: 'Immutable served manifest key: overall or path-based section/content scope; not a mutable UI label']
  score_kind score_kind [not null]
  score numeric(7,2) [not null]
  max_score numeric(7,2) [not null]
  scale text [not null, note: 'points | toeic_section | toeic_total | ielts_band']
  scoring_policy_key text [not null, note: 'Scorer version that produced this score']
  computed_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (attempt_id, scope_key, score_kind) [unique, name: 'uq_attempt_scores_scope_kind']
  }

  checks {
    `max_score > 0 AND score >= 0` [name: 'ck_attempt_scores_range']
  }

  Note: '[P1] Score facts per attempt, stored because conversion tables and AI models change. Validate scope_key against immutable served manifest. Per-skill breakdown is derived from responses + content_version_skills.'
}


// =============================================================================
// 9. AI
// =============================================================================

Table ai_runs {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  tenant_id bigint [not null, ref: > tenants.id]
  job_id uuid [ref: > jobs.id, note: 'Public job this invocation belongs to (retries = more runs)']
  requested_by_user_id bigint [ref: > users.id]
  purpose ai_purpose [not null]
  status execution_status [not null, default: 'queued']
  provider text [not null, note: 'openai | anthropic | google | self_hosted']
  model text [not null]
  model_version text
  prompt_key text [not null, note: 'Prompt template id in code']
  prompt_version text [not null]
  input_refs jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: 'Ids only, for audit: {"attempt_response_id":..} {"source_material_id":..}']
  usage jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: '{input_tokens, output_tokens, cost_usd, latency_ms}']
  error_code text
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  started_at timestamptz
  finished_at timestamptz

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, purpose, created_at) [name: 'ix_ai_runs_tenant_purpose']
    (requested_by_user_id, created_at) [name: 'ix_ai_runs_user', note: 'Per-user quota checks']
    job_id [name: 'ix_ai_runs_job']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Internal provider-call ledger = provenance + cost/quota. Outputs live in the domain rows
that point back here (content versions, evaluations, messages, timelines, comments). Raw
prompts/completions are NOT stored (privacy). Queueing and the public lifecycle are in jobs.
'''
}

Table conversations {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  tenant_id bigint [not null]
  user_id bigint [not null]
  kind text [not null, default: 'tutor', note: 'Registry: tutor; later speaking_partner, study_coach']
  attempt_id bigint [ref: > attempts.id, note: 'Context: opened from a result']
  attempt_response_id bigint [ref: > attempt_responses.id, note: 'Context: "Explain this answer"']
  content_version_id uuid [ref: > content_item_versions.id, note: 'Context outside an attempt (disclosed questions or authoring staff only)']
  title text
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  archived_at timestamptz

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, user_id, updated_at) [name: 'ix_conversations_user']
    attempt_response_id [name: 'ix_conversations_response']
  }

  Note: '[P1] AI assistant thread (tutor today), grounded on the verified answer key + explanation of its context. Private to the learner.'
}

Table conversation_messages {
  id bigint [pk, increment, note: 'DB-assigned monotonic BIGINT identity; use GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY in PostgreSQL migrations']
  conversation_id bigint [not null]
  role message_role [not null]
  body text [not null]
  ai_run_id bigint [ref: > ai_runs.id, note: 'Set for assistant messages']
  grounding jsonb [not null, default: `'[]'::jsonb`, note: 'Cited sources: [{"type":"answer_key","question_version_id":..},{"type":"explanation"}]']
  rating smallint [note: 'Learner feedback: -1 not helpful, 1 helpful']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (conversation_id, created_at) [name: 'ix_conversation_messages_conversation']
  }

  checks {
    `role <> 'assistant' OR ai_run_id IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_conversation_messages_ai_provenance']
    `rating IS NULL OR rating IN (-1, 1)` [name: 'ck_conversation_messages_rating']
  }

  Note: '[P1] Messages in a conversation. Assistant messages always carry provenance; grounding separates "verified answer key" from "AI explanation".'
}

// =============================================================================
// 10. PLATFORM KERNEL
// =============================================================================

Table jobs {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  tenant_id bigint [not null, ref: > tenants.id]
  requested_by_user_id bigint [ref: > users.id, note: 'NULL for system jobs (sweeper, scheduler)']
  kind text [not null, note: 'Registry (API Job.type): question_generation, speech_synthesis, audio_alignment, media_processing, content_assist, quality_check, writing_evaluation, speaking_evaluation, tutor_reply, originality_check, import_validation, material_extraction, manifest_compilation, account_deletion']
  status execution_status [not null, default: 'queued']
  target_type text [note: 'Registry: attempt_response | content_version | content_import | content_submission | media_asset | conversation | user']
  target_key text [note: 'Canonical textual identifier of target_type: decimal BIGINT or lowercase UUID. No FK (heterogeneous target kinds); validated by job handler.']
  input jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: 'Typed per kind; ids and options only, no secrets']
  result jsonb [note: 'Typed per kind; references only']
  progress jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: '{percent, stage}']
  error jsonb [note: '{code, retryable}']
  run_count smallint [not null, default: 0, note: 'Worker executions so far']
  run_after timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  lease_expires_at timestamptz [note: 'Worker lease expiry for reclaiming stalled running jobs; heartbeat extends lease']
  cancel_requested_at timestamptz
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  started_at timestamptz
  finished_at timestamptz

  indexes {
    (status, run_after) [name: 'ix_jobs_queue', note: 'Partial: WHERE status = queued; use FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED when claiming']
    (status, lease_expires_at) [name: 'ix_jobs_stalled', note: 'Partial: WHERE status = running; reclaim only when lease expired']
    (tenant_id, requested_by_user_id, created_at) [name: 'ix_jobs_requester', note: 'Job list + quota counting']
    (target_type, target_key) [name: 'ix_jobs_target']
  }

  checks {
    `(target_type IS NULL) = (target_key IS NULL)` [name: 'ck_jobs_target_pair']
    `run_count >= 0` [name: 'ck_jobs_run_count']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Public async handle with one lifecycle for AI and non-AI work.
Polymorphic (target_type, target_key) is intentionally TEXT + type; never assume all target IDs are UUID. Validate target reference in each handler. Claim queued work by
transactional FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, commit status=running + lease_expires_at, heartbeat
or reclaim expired leases, and use idempotent handlers to tolerate at-least-once execution.
Jobs never mutate published content; outputs land in drafts or permitted domain facts.
Provider calls are recorded per invocation in ai_runs.job_id.
'''
}

Table idempotency_keys {
  principal text [not null, note: 'user:<8-digit id> or anon:<sha256(client fingerprint)> for unauthenticated guest creation']
  key uuid [not null]
  method text [not null]
  path text [not null, note: 'Route template + ids, e.g. /attempts/{id}/submit']
  request_sha256 bytea [not null, note: 'Hash of method + path + canonical body']
  response_status smallint
  response_body jsonb [note: 'Never secrets: token-issuing endpoints store ids only and re-mint on replay']
  locked_until timestamptz [note: 'Set while the first request is in flight']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (principal, key) [pk]
    created_at [name: 'ix_idempotency_keys_expiry', note: 'Purge rows older than 24 h']
  }

  Note: '[P1] Idempotency-Key replay store (24 h). UNLOGGED acceptable: loss degrades to domain-rule duplicate detection.'
}

// =============================================================================
// TENANT-CONSISTENCY, SCOPE & SAME-ITEM COMPOSITE FOREIGN KEYS
// =============================================================================

// Role scope guards
Ref: role_assignments.(role_id, role_scope) > roles.(id, scope)
Ref: action_tokens.(role_id, role_scope) > roles.(id, scope)
Ref: role_permissions.(role_id, role_scope) > roles.(id, scope)
Ref: role_permissions.(permission_id, role_scope) > permissions.(id, scope)

// Session tenant context must be a membership of the session user
Ref: auth_sessions.(active_tenant_id, user_id) > tenant_memberships.(tenant_id, user_id)

// Tenant logo belongs to the tenant
Ref: tenants.(id, logo_asset_id) > media_assets.(tenant_id, id)

// Learner data lives inside a membership
Ref: source_materials.(tenant_id, owner_user_id) > tenant_memberships.(tenant_id, user_id)
Ref: learning_goals.(tenant_id, user_id) > tenant_memberships.(tenant_id, user_id)
Ref: attempts.(tenant_id, user_id) > tenant_memberships.(tenant_id, user_id)
Ref: conversations.(tenant_id, user_id) > tenant_memberships.(tenant_id, user_id)
Ref: content_ratings.(tenant_id, user_id) > tenant_memberships.(tenant_id, user_id)
Ref: content_reports.(reporter_tenant_id, reporter_user_id) > tenant_memberships.(tenant_id, user_id)

// Private content owners and workflow actors are members of the tenant they act in
Ref: content_items.(tenant_id, owner_user_id) > tenant_memberships.(tenant_id, user_id)
Ref: content_imports.(tenant_id, created_by_user_id) > tenant_memberships.(tenant_id, user_id)
Ref: content_submissions.(tenant_id, submitter_user_id) > tenant_memberships.(tenant_id, user_id)

// Content graph: versions belong to their item; published pointer stays on the same item
Ref: content_item_versions.(tenant_id, item_id) > content_items.(tenant_id, id)
Ref: content_items.(id, current_published_version_id) > content_item_versions.(item_id, id)
Ref: content_item_versions.(item_id, based_on_version_id) > content_item_versions.(item_id, id)
Ref: content_item_relations.(tenant_id, parent_version_id) > content_item_versions.(tenant_id, id) [delete: cascade]
Ref: content_item_relations.(child_item_id, child_version_id) > content_item_versions.(item_id, id)
Ref: content_version_assets.(tenant_id, content_version_id) > content_item_versions.(tenant_id, id) [delete: cascade]
Ref: content_version_assets.(tenant_id, asset_id) > media_assets.(tenant_id, id)
Ref: content_media_timelines.content_version_asset_id - content_version_assets.id [delete: cascade]
Ref: content_item_versions.(tenant_id, source_material_id) > source_materials.(tenant_id, id)
Ref: source_materials.(tenant_id, asset_id) > media_assets.(tenant_id, id)

// Learner records pin a consistent (item, version) pair; ratings rate a version of the item
Ref: attempts.(content_item_id, content_version_id) > content_item_versions.(item_id, id)
Ref: content_ratings.(item_id, content_version_id) > content_item_versions.(item_id, id)

// Workflow stays inside the owning tenant
Ref: content_imports.(tenant_id, package_asset_id) > media_assets.(tenant_id, id)
Ref: content_imports.(tenant_id, report_asset_id) > media_assets.(tenant_id, id)
Ref: content_imports.(tenant_id, root_item_id) > content_items.(tenant_id, id)
Ref: content_imports.(tenant_id, root_version_id) > content_item_versions.(tenant_id, id)
Ref: content_imports.(root_item_id, root_version_id) > content_item_versions.(item_id, id)
Ref: content_submissions.(tenant_id, item_id) > content_items.(tenant_id, id)
Ref: content_submissions.(item_id, content_version_id) > content_item_versions.(item_id, id)
Ref: content_comments.(tenant_id, content_version_id) > content_item_versions.(tenant_id, id) [delete: cascade]
Ref: content_comments.(tenant_id, submission_id) > content_submissions.(tenant_id, id) [delete: cascade]

// Compositions (child rows have no meaning without parent)
Ref: conversation_messages.conversation_id > conversations.id [delete: cascade]

// =============================================================================
// TABLE GROUPS
// =============================================================================

TableGroup identity_access [color: #3B82F6] {
  users
  auth_identities
  auth_sessions
  action_tokens
  roles
  permissions
  role_permissions
  role_assignments
  Note: 'Global identity plus typed single-use tokens and unified role assignments.'
}

TableGroup tenancy [color: #8B5CF6] {
  tenants
  tenant_memberships
  tenant_entitlements
  Note: 'Organization boundary, membership, and feature entitlements. Role grants live in identity_access.'
}

TableGroup media [color: #64748B] {
  media_assets
  source_materials
  Note: 'Files in object storage (R2 / MinIO) and learner-uploaded study material.'
}

TableGroup reference [color: #94A3B8] {
  exam_types
  skills
  Note: 'Global, code-seeded reference data: test formats and the skill taxonomy.'
}

TableGroup content_graph [color: #10B981] {
  content_items
  content_item_versions
  content_item_relations
  content_version_assets
  content_media_timelines
  content_answer_specs
  content_version_skills
  Note: 'Logical identity, immutable versions, reusable placements, protected answers/media; manifests compiled to media_assets.'
}

TableGroup content_ecosystem [color: #14B8A6] {
  content_access_grants
  content_credits
  content_ratings
  content_reports
  Note: 'Item-level sharing, attribution, ratings and protected problem reports; counters derived from facts.'
}

TableGroup content_workflow [color: #0EA5E9] {
  content_imports
  content_submissions
  content_comments
  Note: 'Imports, submissions and one append-only feedback/decision/event model.'
}

TableGroup learning [color: #F59E0B] {
  learning_goals
  attempts
  attempt_responses
  attempt_annotations
  evaluations
  attempt_scores
  Note: 'Historical facts of learning, pinned to exact content versions.'
}

TableGroup ai [color: #EC4899] {
  ai_runs
  conversations
  conversation_messages
  Note: 'AI provenance ledger and assistant conversations. Outputs live in domain tables.'
}

TableGroup platform [color: #475569] {
  jobs
  idempotency_keys
  Note: 'Cross-cutting kernel: async jobs and request idempotency.'
}
